## 6. UI / UX principles

### Mobile-first touch
- **+** / **−** minimum ~48–56dp hit targets.
- Bottom **tab bar** on narrow screens (Home, Create, Hub, History, Settings).
- Wide screens: collapsible **sidebar** + multi-column goal grid (current direction is fine).

### Visual feedback
- Animate progress changes (Reanimated / layout animations)—no cold snaps when values change.
- Completion state: subtle success tint on card.
- Overflow state: distinct from “exactly 100%” (e.g. accent ring, “Over target” chip).

### Web layout
- Content max width where reading matters (forms ~720–800px).
- Dashboard grid can span wider (2–5 columns by breakpoint)—not forced to 600px phone column on desktop.
- Static web: fix deprecated Clipboard usage (`expo-clipboard`); ensure paste import works on all major browsers.

### Accessibility (v1 minimum)
- Text labels on icon-only buttons.
- Sufficient contrast in light/dark.
- Don’t rely on color alone for completed vs incomplete.

### Theming
- Centralized tokens (`useAppTheme` / theme constants).
- User preference persisted; respect system when set to System.

